# Line endings, stated rather than left to whatever each clone has configured.
#
# `text=auto` is what this repository was already doing by accident: LF in the index,
# native in the working tree. Measured before writing this -- 54 of 57 tracked files were
# `i/lf w/crlf`. Saying it here changes nothing about the current tree and stops a
# contributor whose core.autocrlf differs from committing CRLF into the index, which is
# the failure this prevents.
#
# Deliberately NOT `eol=lf`: that would rewrite every working copy on Windows for no gain.
* text=auto

# Binary, so git never tries to diff or normalise it. `text=auto` above would almost
# certainly detect these anyway, but "almost certainly" is not what you want standing
# between a demo recording and CRLF translation.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
